---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
---

<PageLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Read the PROJECT: automate Privacy Policy to learn how we collect, use, and protect the personal information you share with us."
>
	<section class="section legal">
		<div class="container legal-wrap">
			<SectionHeading eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" subtitle="Last Updated: August 2026" />

			<p><strong>Project Automate Inc.</strong>, doing business as <strong>PROJECT: automate</strong>, respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal information you provide when visiting our website or using our services. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information.</p>

			<h2>Interpretation and Definitions</h2>
			<h3>Interpretation</h3>
			<p>The words with the first letter capitalized have meanings defined under the following conditions. These definitions shall have the same meaning regardless of whether they appear in singular or plural.</p>

			<h3>Definitions</h3>
			<p>For the purposes of this Privacy Policy:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Company</strong> refers to Project Automate Inc., doing business as PROJECT: automate.</li>
				<li><strong>Website</strong> refers to <a href="https://projectautomate.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://projectautomate.com</a>.</li>
				<li><strong>Personal Information</strong> means any information that identifies or can be used to identify an individual, such as name, email address, phone number, or other contact information.</li>
				<li><strong>Service</strong> refers to the website, services, consultations, installations, and support provided by Project Automate Inc.</li>
				<li><strong>You</strong> means the individual accessing the website or using our services.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>SMS Privacy</h2>
			<p>Mobile information, phone numbers, and SMS opt-in consent will not be sold, rented, or shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.</p>
			<p>Information may be shared with service providers only when necessary to deliver requested communications and operate our messaging services. These providers may not use the information for their own marketing purposes.</p>

			<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
			<p>We may collect the following types of information when you interact with our website or services:</p>

			<h3>Personal Information</h3>
			<p>You may voluntarily provide information including:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Name</li>
				<li>Email address</li>
				<li>Phone number</li>
				<li>Project details or inquiry information</li>
			</ul>
			<p>This information is typically collected when you:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Submit a contact form</li>
				<li>Request a consultation</li>
				<li>Communicate with us via email or phone</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>Automatically Collected Information</h3>
			<p>When you visit our website, certain information may automatically be collected including:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>IP address</li>
				<li>Browser type</li>
				<li>Device information</li>
				<li>Pages visited on our website</li>
				<li>Date and time of visits</li>
			</ul>
			<p>This information helps us improve our website performance and user experience.</p>

			<h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
			<p>PROJECT: automate uses the information collected for the following purposes:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>To respond to inquiries and provide consultations</li>
				<li>To communicate regarding services or projects</li>
				<li>To improve our website and services</li>
				<li>To provide customer support</li>
				<li>To send relevant updates or service-related communications</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Sharing Your Information</h2>
			<p>PROJECT: automate does <strong>not sell or rent personal information</strong> to third parties.</p>
			<p>We may share information only in limited circumstances such as:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>With trusted service providers who assist in operating our website or services</li>
				<li>When required by law or legal obligations</li>
			</ul>
			<p>These partners are required to protect your information and use it only for the services they provide.</p>

			<h2>Data Security</h2>
			<p>We take reasonable security measures to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, disclosure, or misuse.</p>
			<p>However, no method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

			<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
			<p>Our website and services are not directed toward individuals under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>
			<p>If we become aware that personal information has been collected from a child without parental consent, we will take steps to remove that information.</p>

			<h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
			<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with the updated revision date.</p>
			<p>We encourage users to review this page periodically to stay informed about how we protect their information.</p>

			<h2>SMS Data Sharing and Transfers</h2>
			<p>Consumer SMS registration data, mobile phone numbers, and SMS consent or opt-in information are not sold, rented, shared, transferred, or disclosed to external organizations, affiliates, service providers, or other third parties for marketing or promotional purposes.</p>
			<p>SMS consent and opt-in data will not be transferred to external organizations except when disclosure is required by law.</p>
			<p>You may opt out of receiving SMS messages from PROJECT: automate at any time by replying STOP to any message.</p>
			<p>For assistance, reply HELP to any message or contact us directly:</p>
			<p>Phone: 1-310-402-4818<br />Email: <a href="mailto:support@projectautomate.com">support@projectautomate.com</a></p>

			<h2>Contact Us</h2>
			<p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or how your information is handled, please contact us:</p>
			<p>
				Project Automate Inc., doing business as PROJECT: automate<br />
				Website: <a href="https://projectautomate.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://projectautomate.com</a><br />
				Email: <a href="mailto:sales@projectautomate.com">sales@projectautomate.com</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
	.legal-wrap {
		max-width: 780px;
		padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-24);
	}

	.legal-wrap h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-2xl);
		margin-top: var(--space-12);
		padding-top: var(--space-8);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.legal-wrap h2:first-of-type {
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
		padding-top: 0;
		border-top: none;
	}

	.legal-wrap h3 {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
	}

	.legal-wrap p {
		max-width: 68ch;
	}

	.legal-wrap p a,
	.legal-wrap li a {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}
	.legal-wrap p a:hover,
	.legal-wrap li a:hover {
		color: var(--color-accent-hover);
	}

	.legal-wrap ul {
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
		max-width: 68ch;
	}

	.legal-wrap li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: var(--space-6);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.legal-wrap li::before {
		content: '—';
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}
</style>
